EXPERIMENT 1: LIBRARY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM
1. AIM
To design and develop a Library Management System using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript to manage books, student accounts, borrowing history, fines, and study materials.
2. ALGORITHM
1. Start the program.
2. Create a webpage with a book catalog, student account, study materials, and admin panel.
3. Design the webpage using HTML elements and CSS styling.
4. Display available books with their titles, authors, and categories.
5. Allow users to search for books by title or author.
6. Provide student registration and login forms.
7. Display borrowing history and calculate fines based on overdue days.
8. Allow the administrator to add books to the library.
9. Provide year-wise and semester-wise study material filtering.
10. Display the results dynamically using JavaScript.
3. HTML CODE
Filename: experiment1_library.html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Library Management System</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="experiment1_library.css">
</head>
<body>

<header>
    <div>
        <h1>📚 Campus Library</h1>
        <p>Books, borrowing and study materials in one place</p>
    </div>
    <button onclick="showTab('admin')">Admin Panel</button>
</header>

<nav>
    <button onclick="showTab('books')">Book Catalog</button>
    <button onclick="showTab('account')">Student Account</button>
    <button onclick="showTab('materials')">Study Materials</button>
    <button onclick="showTab('admin')">Manage Library</button>
</nav>

<main>

    <!-- Book Catalog -->
    <section id="books" class="panel">
        <h2>Find a Book</h2>

        <div class="controls">
            <input type="text" id="bookSearch"
                   placeholder="Search title or author..."
                   oninput="renderBooks()">
            <button onclick="renderBooks()">Search</button>
        </div>

        <div id="bookList" class="cards"></div>
    </section>

    <!-- Student Account -->
    <section id="account" class="panel hidden">
        <h2>Student Account</h2>

        <div class="grid2">

            <form id="registerForm" class="card">
                <h3>Register / Login</h3>

                <input type="text" id="studentName"
                       placeholder="Student name" required>

                <input type="email" id="studentEmail"
                       placeholder="Email address" required>

                <input type="password" id="studentPassword"
                       placeholder="Password" required>

                <button type="submit">Register / Login</button>

                <p id="loginMessage" class="message"></p>
            </form>

            <div class="card">
                <h3>My Borrow History</h3>
                <p>Issue date and expected return date are shown below.</p>

                <div id="borrowList"></div>

                <h3>Fine Checker</h3>

                <label>
                    Days overdue
                    <input type="number" id="lateDays"
                           min="0" value="0">
                </label>

                <button onclick="calculateFine()">Calculate Fine</button>

                <p id="fineOutput" class="message">Fine: ₹0</p>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Study Materials -->
    <section id="materials" class="panel hidden">
        <h2>Study Materials</h2>

        <div class="controls">
            <select id="yearFilter">
                <option value="">All years</option>
                <option>1st Year</option>
                <option>2nd Year</option>
                <option>3rd Year</option>
                <option>4th Year</option>
            </select>

            <select id="semesterFilter">
                <option value="">All semesters</option>
                <option>Semester 1</option>
                <option>Semester 2</option>
            </select>

            <button onclick="renderMaterials()">Search Materials</button>
        </div>

        <div id="materialList" class="cards"></div>
    </section>

    <!-- Admin Panel -->
    <section id="admin" class="panel hidden">
        <h2>Admin: Manage Books</h2>

        <form id="bookForm" class="formrow">
            <input type="text" id="newTitle"
                   placeholder="Book title" required>

            <input type="text" id="newAuthor"
                   placeholder="Author" required>

            <input type="text" id="newCategory"
                   placeholder="Category" required>

            <button type="submit">Add Book</button>
        </form>

        <div id="adminBookList"></div>
    </section>

</main>

<footer>
    Campus Library • Internet Programming Lab
</footer>

<script src="experiment1_library.js"></script>

</body>
</html>

